<title>USA: NYSE Unavailables -.</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavailables -.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Tuesday Mid-American Waste Systems Inc, Capital Re Corp, MCN Corp, International Business Machines and IBM preferred A stock were not available for after-hours trading for news.</p>
<p>Mid-American filed for Chapter 11 protection, while the other three companies reported quarterly earnings.</p>
<p>IBM reported fourth-quarter earnings of $3.93 a share against $3.09 a year ago.</p>
<p>The exchange said Corimon SACA , Westmoreland Coal Co, Westmoreland preferred A stock and Echlin Inc were also unavailable for trading.</p>
